    "id": "crossing",
    "title": "Tickets, memories, please",
    "description": "The train slips above the sleeping city. A passenger unfolds a ticket with your name on it. Beyond the glass, the night is beginning to crack. The suitcase opens a finger’s width, and something inside asks to be let out.",
    "objective": "Learn what the sunrise wants. Choose what you are willing to trade for it.",
    "gmNotes": "The nameless passenger is a future version of someone at the table. They want the sunrise released, but believe it will erase their journey. Offer three leads: a ticket remembers its buyer, the conductor knows the price, the suitcase speaks when addressed with kindness. Let the players choose a fourth.",
